 "script": "estimate/sensor_offsets.py",
 "method": "(acceleration against acceleration, 50 Hz):\n- device: |a| minus its 1-s moving median (removes gravity), absolute value, 0.2-s moving mean;\n- marker: position smoothed over 0.1 s, second derivative, magnitude, 0.2-s moving mean; samples\n  next to a marker jump (speed > 3000 mm/s) are dropped;\n- both rank-transformed (Spearman correlation, robust to marker spikes);\n- coarse search +-20 s on a 10-Hz copy, then fine search +-0.5 s at 0.02 s on the whole recording;\n- the same fine search on every 120-s window (+-1 s around the global value) -> median over windows,\n  90 % interval by bootstrap over windows (1 000 resamples), drift = slope of window lag vs time\n  multiplied by the recording length.\nSign: lag > 0 means the device is LATE; aligning means device_aligned[t] = device[t + lag].",
 "rule": "shift only if the whole 90 % interval is outside +-0.1 s; rounded to samples",
 "gate": {
  "r_min": 0.5,
  "ci_width_max_s": 0.2,
  "drift_max_s": 0.1
 },
 "sign": "lag > 0: device late; aligned[t] = raw[t + lag]",
